T:What it is
T:A mountain
T:is an
T:elevated
T:portion of
T:the surface
T:of a planet,
T:generally
T:with steep
T:sides that
T:show
T:significant
T:exposed
T:bedrock.
T:Although
T:there are no
T:universally
T:accepted
T:definitions,
T:a mountain
T:is usually
T:considered
T:higher than
T:a hill. By
T:definition,
T:mountains
T:are often
T:thought of
T:as being a
T:landform
T:which is
T:higher than
T:2,000 feet
T:(610 m). It
T:may either
T:have a
T:limited
T:summit area
T:or be a
T:smaller
T:plateau with
T:high
T:elevation
T:and steep
T:sides. A few
T:mountains
T:are isolated
T:summits, but
T:most occur
T:in mountain
T:ranges.
